#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
"""App CI gate (contract sdk/contracts/poc-v0.md §9.4 checks 2-9) -> apps/<id>/scan.json (§11.1).

Per app:
  1+8  schema, id, kustomize build | kubeconform, limits, pins (sdk/tools/validate-apps)
  2    licence class from GitHub's SPDX id + research-output/evidence/license-matrix.csv
  3    every image tag+digest pinned; the digest's index has every declared spec.archs (crane)
  4+6  Trivy over each image and declared arch: CVEs (CRITICAL with a fix fails) and secrets
  5    ClamAV over each image's exported filesystem (`crane export`); any hit fails and blocks
  7    cosign verify when the upstream signs (else "unsigned"); OpenSSF Scorecard (informational);
       archived upstream or no release in 18 months caps the tier at community
  8    non-root where the image allows it
  9    --smoke: install into namespace app-<id> with the current kubectl context, wait for
       rollout, HTTP 200/3xx from spec.web.port (skipped when the app has no spec.web)

Run with: python3 -I sdk/tools/app-gate [options] APP_ID [APP_ID ...]
Exit codes: 0 every app passes, 1 at least one app fails, 2 usage or environment error.
With --fail-on claim (pull requests), 1 means only that a committed claim is higher than the gate's
verdict: metadata.tier above the computed tier, or a committed scan.json saying "pass" for an app
that fails. An app that honestly fails (tier blocked or community, scan.json not "pass") can merge;
the gateway refuses to install it (§10.3, §11.1).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

